Why: the Chromium/Electron accessibility wait also looks for web content in the app's windows on another Space, so the first read of such an app whose windows are all off-Space returns at once instead of waiting out the 4 s timeout (up to three times per app lifetime).

ensure_chromium_ax_enabled waits, after turning on AXManualAccessibility,
until an AXWebArea appears under the application element. Windows on another
Space are not among its children, so for an app whose windows are all there
(the user works in a full-screen app) the probe never sees the web content
that is already built, and every first read paid MATERIALIZE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS
(measured: 4.96 s for a get_window_state of an Electron app), then again on
each of the retries. The off-Space windows are resolved once per attempt with
the same lookup copy_ax_windows_including uses (new copy_off_space_windows,
at most 8), and the probe checks them after the application element. Without
off-Space windows nothing changes. Upstreamable as is.

